  "description" : "Layer updated by OCHA-CI in collaboration with CNTIG.Source: Comité National de Télédétection et d'Information Géographique (CNTIG)Contributor: OCHA West and Central Africa (ROWCA)Reference Period: August 06, 2018-September 20, 2023Updated: 4 April 2023Expected Update Frequency: Every yearLocation: Côte d'IvoireLicense: Creative Commons Attribution for Intergovernmental OrganisationsMethodology: Quality assured, configured, and published as live services by ITOS.Caveats / Comments:  The edge-matched layers are subject to the following potential limitations:Where countries border each other, one or even both boundaries may be less accurate than the original, definitive boundaries. The UN Geospatial Hub boundary is generally of lower quality than the definitive COD-AB layers.Peripheral polygon feature shapes and the relationship of their areas to those of their internal neighbouring features may be distorted, while internal features are untouched.Peripheral polygon features may artificially appear to touch different, incorrect features belonging the same country.*In theory, peripheral polygon features may be eliminated. This is monitored and will be specially treated if it occurs.", 
